window.AG_CHAPTERS["08"] = {"id":"08","title":"The Ferryman&#39;s Winter","titleZh":"船家的冬天","patient":{"name":"Old Cheng 程老","sprite":"man"},"scene":{"img":"art/scene-river.jpg","key":"river"},"pattern":"Phlegm-Heat Obstructing the Lung 痰熱壅肺","principle":"clear heat, transform phlegm, and free the Lung to descend","tongue":"red body, yellow greasy coating","pulseNote":{"en":"It rolls under the finger like a bead on a plate, and it comes fast.","zh":"往來流利，如珠走盤，且來去甚速"},"needleAsk":{"en":"Needle <b>Chǐzé LU5</b>. Tap its exact location.","zh":"行針 — 點出穴位精確位置"},"target":{"id":"LU5","zh":"尺澤","py":"Chǐzé","x":160,"y":158,"img":"art/body-forearm-palmar.jpg","w":434,"h":1159,"decoys":[{"x":140,"y":652},{"x":185,"y":571},{"x":150,"y":610},{"x":230,"y":300},{"x":120,"y":420}],"note":"<b>尺澤 Chǐzé LU5</b> — on the cubital crease, in the depression on the radial side of the biceps tendon. Sea point of the Lung.<br>肘橫紋中，肱二頭肌腱橈側凹陷處。肺經合穴。"},"hints":{"ask":{"en":"Ask what he coughs up. Colour and thickness will settle this case faster than anything else.","zh":"問其所咯之痰。色與稠度，較他症更能決斷。"},"look":{"en":"Two things on the tongue, and you need both: the colour of the body, and whether the coating is greasy.","zh":"舌有二事，缺一不可：舌質之色，與苔之膩否。"},"pulse":{"en":"Something substantial is moving in the vessel, and it is moving fast.","zh":"脈中有形之物在行，且行之甚速。"},"dx":{"en":"Excess or deficiency → interior or exterior → and then name both pathogens, because there are two.","zh":"虛實 → 表裡 → 而後並舉其邪，蓋邪有二。"},"rx":{"en":"Two pathogens need two answers. Clear the heat, and transform the phlegm — one point cannot do both well.","zh":"二邪當有二治：清其熱，化其痰。一穴難以兼擅。"},"tech":{"en":"A full pattern is drained. Ask also whether warming has any place here at all.","zh":"實證當瀉。且當自問：此證溫法尚有可用之處否？"}},"reactions":[{"who":"master","en":"Master Shen tilts his head at the sound of the cough. \"Loud. Go on.\"","zh":"參師父側耳聽那咳聲。「聲重。繼續。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"Old Cheng thumps his own chest twice, out of habit.","zh":"程老習慣性地捶了兩下胸口。"},{"who":"boy","en":"The herb boy opens the window a hand's width.","zh":"藥童把窗推開一掌寬。"},{"who":"master","en":"\"He has been on the river all winter. But this is not the cold you saw in chapter one.\"","zh":"「他整個冬天都在河上。然此非第一章之寒。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"\"It's the thick stuff that won't come up,\" he says. \"Sits on my chest like a stone.\"","zh":"「就是那口稠痰咯不上來，」他說，「壓在胸口像塊石頭。」"},{"who":"master","en":"\"Cold that stays turns to heat. Heat that stays cooks the fluids into phlegm. Ask what colour it is now.\"","zh":"「寒久化熱，熱久煉液成痰。問他如今是什麼顏色。」"}],"remedy":{"ask":"cold_heat","look":"cold_heat","pulse":"cold_heat","dx":"excess_def","rx":"channel_organ","tech":"excess_def"},"reward":{"cardEn":"Clear and Transform","cardZh":"清熱化痰","cardTxt":"When two pathogens are tangled together, name both and treat both. Clearing heat without transforming phlegm leaves the obstruction; transforming phlegm without clearing heat leaves the fire that made it.","herbId":"chenpi","herbEn":"Aged Tangerine Peel","herbZh":"陳皮","herbImg":"art/card-chenpi.jpg","sprite":"art/sprite-renshen-jump.webp","herbTxt":"Acrid, bitter and warm. It regulates qi and transforms phlegm — in a hot pattern it is paired with cooling herbs, so that the phlegm moves without the warmth adding to the heat."},"endings":{"three":["Ten days later Old Cheng brings the herb boy a fish. \"The stone's gone,\" he says. \"Phlegm comes up white now, and thin.\"<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You named two pathogens instead of one. Most students see the heat, treat the heat, and leave the phlegm sitting there.\"","十日後，程老送了藥童一條魚。「石頭沒了，」他說，「現在痰是白的，也稀了。」<br><b>參師父：</b>「你舉了二邪而非一邪。多數學生只見其熱，治其熱，卻把痰留在原處。」"],"two":["The fever settles but the chest still feels loaded.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You cleared the heat. What made the phlegm is gone; the phlegm is not.\"","熱退了，胸中仍覺壅滿。<br><b>參師父：</b>「你清了熱。生痰者已去，痰卻還在。」"],"one":["No better, and he is short of breath climbing the bank.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"Yellow and thick. You were told in the first answer. What did you do with it?\"","未見好轉，上岸都喘。<br><b>參師父：</b>「黃而稠。第一問就告訴你了。你拿它做了什麼？」"],"titles":["Old Cheng Breathes Easy","Old Cheng Is Cooler","Old Cheng Will Need Another Visit"]},"script":[{"w":"master","en":"You have met a cough from cold, and a cough from dryness. This is a third kind entirely.","cn":"你見過寒咳，也見過燥咳。這是第三種，全然不同。"},{"w":"patient","en":"Doctor. Cheng. I pole the ferry. Started as a chill three weeks back, now it's settled into my chest.","cn":"大夫。姓程，撐渡船的。三週前著了涼，如今落到胸裡去了。"},{"w":"patient","en":"I cough till I'm bent double. It's thick and it's yellow, and I'm hot with it.","cn":"咳得直不起腰。痰稠而黃，人還發熱。"},{"w":"master","en":"Three weeks. It began on the surface and it has gone inward and turned. That is the ordinary course of things.","cn":"三週。始於表而入於裡，且已化熱。此病之常。"},{"w":"master","en":"Now there are two pathogens in his chest, not one. Find them both.","cn":"如今其胸中有二邪，非一邪。二者俱要問出來。"}],"qa":[{"q":"What does the phlegm look like?","cq":"痰是什麼樣子？","good":1,"a":"Thick, yellow, and it sticks. I have to fight to bring it up.","ca":"稠、黃、黏，得使勁才咯得出。","clue":{"en":"Thick yellow phlegm","zh":"痰黃稠"},"note":"Thick and yellow is heat that has cooked the fluids. Thin and white would be cold; scanty and sticky would be dryness. Colour and thickness carry most of the diagnosis in a cough. 稠黃者，熱煉津液所成。稀白為寒，少黏為燥。咳嗽之辨，多在痰之色質。"},{"q":"Do you have a fever, and are you thirsty?","cq":"發熱嗎？口渴嗎？","good":1,"a":"Warm most of the day, and I want cold water.","ca":"整日身熱，想喝涼水。","clue":{"en":"Fever, thirst for cold drinks","zh":"發熱、渴喜冷飲"},"note":"Fever with a wish for cold confirms real heat with substance behind it — unlike empty heat, which comes in the afternoon and brings no great thirst. 發熱而喜冷飲，為有形實熱。虛熱則午後而作，亦不甚渴。"},{"q":"Does your chest hurt, and is your breathing tight?","cq":"胸痛嗎？氣促嗎？","good":1,"a":"It aches when I cough hard, and I'm short of wind going up the bank.","ca":"咳重了胸口就痛，上岸也喘。","clue":{"en":"Chest pain, shortness of breath","zh":"胸痛、氣促"},"note":"Phlegm is substantial: it occupies the chest, blocks the Lung's descent and hurts when the ribcage works. That obstruction is what distinguishes phlegm-heat from plain heat. 痰為有形，據於胸中，阻肺之肅降，咳動則痛。此壅塞正是痰熱與單純熱證之別。"},{"q":"Do you still feel chilled, or averse to wind?","cq":"還怕冷、惡風嗎？","good":1,"a":"Not now. That was the first week.","ca":"現在不了。那是頭一週的事。","clue":{"en":"No aversion to cold now","zh":"已不惡寒"},"note":"The exterior stage has passed. While chills and fever coexist the pathogen is still on the surface; once chills go and heat remains, it has moved inward. 表證已罷。惡寒發熱並見者邪尚在表；寒去熱存，則邪已入裡。"},{"q":"Do you sweat at night and feel warm in the afternoons?","cq":"夜間盜汗嗎？午後潮熱嗎？","good":0,"a":"No. I'm hot all day, not just afternoons. And I sweat because I'm hot.","ca":"沒有。我是整天熱，不只午後。出汗是因為熱。","clue":"","note":"A good exclusion. Those two findings would point to yin deficiency — the previous patient's pattern. All-day heat with thick phlegm is the opposite. 排除得當。此二症屬陰虛，即前一病人之證。終日發熱兼痰稠，適與之相反。"},{"q":"Are your stools loose and your limbs heavy?","cq":"便溏嗎？肢體沉重嗎？","good":0,"a":"Stools are firm. Limbs are fine.","ca":"大便成形。手腳沒事。","clue":"","note":"Checking for damp encumbering the Spleen — reasonable, but negative. The phlegm here sits in the chest, not the middle burner. 察濕困脾，問得合理，惟為陰性。本案之痰在胸，不在中焦。"}],"look":[{"t":"Red body with a yellow greasy coating","c":"舌紅、苔黃膩","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Red tongue, yellow greasy coat","zh":"舌紅苔黃膩"},"note":"Correct, and it is exactly two findings for two pathogens. Red body = heat. Greasy coat = phlegm-damp with substance. Yellow and greasy together is phlegm that has been cooked. 是，二象正應二邪。舌紅主熱，苔膩主有形痰濕。黃而膩者，痰已化熱。"},{"t":"Red body with little coating","c":"舌紅少苔","ok":0,"note":"That is empty heat from yin deficiency — dry, with scanty sticky phlegm. His phlegm is copious and thick. 此為陰虛虛熱，燥而痰少黏。本案痰多而稠。"},{"t":"Pale body with a white greasy coat","c":"舌淡、苔白膩","ok":0,"note":"Cold-damp phlegm. The phlegm is right; the temperature is not. White phlegm, no fever, no thirst. 此為寒痰濕。痰是對的，寒熱不對：痰白、不發熱、不口渴。"},{"t":"Pale body with a thin white coat","c":"舌淡苔薄白","ok":0,"note":"Wind-cold on the exterior, or Lung qi deficiency. Neither fits a man with a yellow tongue coat and three weeks of fever. 此為風寒表證或肺氣虛。其苔黃、發熱三週，皆不合。"}],"pulse":[{"t":"Slippery and rapid 滑數","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Slippery rapid pulse","zh":"脈滑數"},"note":"Correct, and again two readings for two pathogens. Slippery: something substantial rolls in the vessel — phlegm. Rapid: heat. 是，一脈而應二邪。滑者脈中有形之物往來，痰也；數者熱也。"},{"t":"Thready and rapid 細數","ok":0,"note":"Thready means the vessel is under-filled — deficiency. His pulse is full and rolling, not narrow. 細者脈道不充，虛也。本案脈滑而盛，非細。"},{"t":"Floating and rapid 浮數","ok":0,"note":"That is wind-heat still on the exterior. He stopped feeling chilled two weeks ago. 此為風熱在表。其惡寒已止兩週。"},{"t":"Wiry 弦","ok":0,"note":"The Liver's pulse. Nothing in this case points at the Liver. 肝之本脈。本案無肝證可指。"}],"dx":[{"ask":"Step 1 — excess or deficiency?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第一步：虛實何屬？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Excess","c":"實","ok":1,"note":"Loud forceful cough, copious thick phlegm, fever with thirst, a greasy coat and a full rolling pulse. Every sign has substance and force behind it. 咳聲重濁有力、痰多而稠、發熱口渴、苔膩、脈滑而盛。諸象皆有形有力。"},{"t":"Deficiency","c":"虛","ok":0,"note":"Deficiency is quiet: weak cough, scanty phlegm, a thin or peeling coat, a pulse without force. This is the opposite of all four. 虛證其象靜：咳聲低弱、痰少、苔薄或剝、脈無力。本案四者皆反。"},{"t":"Mixed — an excess pathogen on a deficient base","c":"虛實夾雜","ok":0,"note":"Possible in an older man, and worth watching for as he recovers. But right now nothing is empty: no fatigue, no spontaneous sweating, no weak pulse. 年高者確可如此，病退時尤當留意。然此刻無虛象：不倦、不自汗、脈不弱。"}]},{"ask":"Step 2 — exterior or interior?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第二步：在表在裡？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Interior — the pathogen has moved inward and turned to heat","c":"裡 — 邪已入裡化熱","ok":1,"note":"Chills and fever together means the surface; chills gone and heat remaining means inside. It began three weeks ago as a chill on the river — you are watching the ordinary progression of an exterior pathogen inward. 惡寒發熱並見在表；寒去熱存則入裡。三週前河上受寒而起，此正外邪傳裡之常。"},{"t":"Exterior — wind-heat invading the Lung","c":"表 — 風熱犯肺","ok":0,"note":"Wind-heat on the exterior brings fever with aversion to wind, a sore throat and a floating rapid pulse, in the first days. His is deep and slippery, and the chills stopped a fortnight ago. 風熱在表當見發熱惡風、咽痛、脈浮數，且在初起數日。本案脈滑而不浮，惡寒已止半月。"},{"t":"Half exterior, half interior","c":"半表半裡","ok":0,"note":"That is alternating chills and fever with a bitter mouth and a wiry pulse — Shaoyang. He has neither. 此為往來寒熱、口苦、脈弦之少陽證。本案皆無。"}]},{"ask":"Step 3 — name the pathogens. There are two.<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第三步：舉其邪。邪有二。</small>","opts":[{"t":"Phlegm and heat, tangled together and blocking the Lung","c":"痰與熱互結，壅塞於肺","ok":1,"note":"<b>Two pathogens, and this chapter exists to make you name both.</b> Heat alone would give fever and thirst but no obstruction. Phlegm alone would block the chest but bring no fever. Yellow thick phlegm, a greasy yellow coat and a slippery rapid pulse are the two of them cooked into one. 二邪並見，本章之設，正為使你並舉之。單熱則發熱口渴而無壅塞；單痰則胸滿而不發熱。痰黃稠、苔黃膩、脈滑數，二者已煉為一。"},{"t":"Heat alone","c":"單為熱邪","ok":0,"note":"Then where does the thick phlegm come from, and why is the coat greasy? Heat alone does not obstruct the chest. 若單為熱，稠痰何來？苔何以膩？熱不自壅胸。"},{"t":"Phlegm-damp alone","c":"單為痰濕","ok":0,"note":"Then the phlegm would be white and thin, there would be no fever, no thirst, and the coat would be white. 若單為痰濕，痰當白稀、不發熱、不口渴、苔當白。"}]}],"rx":[{"id":"LU5","t":"Chǐzé LU5 尺澤","ok":1,"note":"Sea point of the Lung and its principal draining point. Sea points govern rebellious qi and diarrhoea, and here it clears Lung heat and sends coughing qi back down. 肺經合穴，瀉肺之主穴。「合主逆氣而泄」，清肺熱、降肺氣，正合本證。"},{"id":"ST40","t":"Fēnglóng ST40 豐隆","ok":1,"note":"The phlegm point. Heat is only half the problem — this is the half that removes the substance. Clearing heat without this leaves the chest still loaded. 化痰要穴。熱僅其半，此穴所去者其形也。徒清其熱而不化其痰，胸中仍壅。"},{"id":"LU10","t":"Yújì LU10 魚際","ok":1,"note":"Spring point of the Lung — Spring points clear heat. It is the point for a hot Lung with a sore throat and a hard cough. 肺經滎穴。「滎主身熱」，肺熱咽痛、咳劇者取之。"},{"id":"LU9","t":"Tàiyuān LU9 太淵","ok":0,"note":"Source point of the Lung, and it <b>tonifies</b>. Tonifying while a substantial pathogen is still lodged in the chest shuts the door with the thief inside — 閉門留寇. 肺之原穴，主補。邪實未去而先補之，是閉門留寇。"},{"id":"KI3","t":"Tàixī KI3 太谿","ok":0,"note":"Nourishes Kidney yin. Right for the dry cough of the last patient; wrong here, and enriching yin can make phlegm stickier. 滋腎陰。宜於前案之燥咳，於此則非，且滋膩反助其痰。"},{"id":"SP9","t":"Yīnlíngquán SP9 陰陵泉","ok":0,"note":"Drains damp from the lower burner. The obstruction here is phlegm in the chest — right idea, wrong floor of the house. 利下焦之濕。本案痰壅在胸，理雖近而部位不合。"}],"tech":[{"t":"Reducing method, and no moxa","c":"瀉法，不施灸","ok":1,"note":"Correct on both counts. A full pattern is drained — firm technique, and the pathogen has somewhere to go. And <b>moxa is warming</b>: adding heat to a man with fever, thirst and yellow phlegm works directly against the treatment principle, however comforting the warmth feels. 二者皆是。實則瀉之，手法宜實，使邪有出路。灸性溫：其人發熱口渴痰黃，加溫適與治則相悖，縱使溫之覺舒。"},{"t":"Reducing method with moxa to open the chest","c":"瀉法，兼灸以通胸陽","ok":0,"note":"Moxa opens a <b>cold</b> obstructed chest. This chest is hot and obstructed — the two look similar from outside and want opposite treatments. 灸以通寒痹之胸陽。本案胸中壅而熱，外貌相似而治法相反。"},{"t":"Reinforcing method, since he is old and three weeks ill","c":"補法，因其年高病久","ok":0,"note":"Age and duration are worth weighing, but you do not tonify while a substantial pathogen is lodged. Clear it first, then rebuild. 年高病久誠當顧慮，然邪實未去不可遽補。先去其邪，後補其正。"},{"t":"Prick LU11 to bleed for the heat","c":"少商點刺放血以泄熱","ok":0,"note":"Defensible as an adjunct for an acute hot throat — but it is not the main answer here, and it does nothing to the phlegm, which is half of what ails him. 急性咽喉熱毒可為輔法，然非本案主治，且於痰無所益——而痰居其半。"}]};
